ib/screens/offer_screen.dart`. The write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nChoices I made where the spec was open:\n- **Email, phone and terms fire once per visit.** The spec says \"started typing\" and \"ticked\", so I read these as the first occurrence.\n- **Slider fires on `onChangeEnd`, once per drag, with the final amount.** The spec says \"moved\", and `onChanged` fires on every step.\n- **`offers_scrolled` fires when a scroll settles** (`ScrollEndNotification`), not on every scroll update.\n- **Continue is only tracked when the button is enabled.** A disabled tap sends nothing.\n\nFrom the colleague's note, I applied the once-only flags, the `onChangeEnd` pattern and the scroll-end pattern. I didn't apply the focus-lost pattern, because no spec event needs a text field's final value. `ANSWER.md` lists this in full.\n\nTwo things to check:\n- `README.md` still says the screens send no events. That's now out of date, and I left it alone.\n- `lib/analytics.dart` still has the `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI` placeholder key, so nothing reaches PostHog until CI supplies the real key.","ttft_ms":1113,"type":"result","duration_ms":232124,"uuid":"f425d986-2a88-4e65-8742-03b43fe1892a","ttft_stream_ms":999,"time_to_request_ms":27,"first_content_frame_ms":999,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":14873,"cacheReadInputTokens":531243,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27407,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.01823353,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5601,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
